WEBVTT

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:19.200
<i>C'mon, morning's here--time to be on our way</i>

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.700
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.830
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>No turning back: this trip is nonfiction</i>

00:00:29.830 --> 00:00:35.080
<i>You ready or not? Ready or not, go!</i>
<i>It's now or never, the real deal: Ready, and... action!</i>

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:40.540
<i>Harsh winds that make us hesitate,</i>
<i>nights spent crying our eyes out</i>

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.790
<i>They're not necessarily bad things (not bad)</i>

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:51.500
<i>Just like the power in a spring:</i>
<i>the harder we're pushed</i>

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.040
<i>The higher we can fly</i>

00:00:55.040 --> 00:01:05.580
<i>Face the far-off distance</i>
<i>and aim for the horizon: rising sun</i>

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.870
<i>Holding our hands up to that morning sun</i>

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:21.250
<i>Our shared feelings brought us together--</i>
<i>we're not alone anymore</i>

00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:27.450
<i>And so we're on this brilliant voyage</i>

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:34.250
<i>Smiling faces, courage,</i>
<i>we're bustin' out: glory days!</i>

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:41.500
Under the rule of Ei Sei,
the King who worked toward unification,

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.620
the Kingdom of Chin launched
an invasion of the land of Gi.

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:48.750
Their opponent: the legendary general Ren Pa.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:51.540
The young commanders stepped
onto a relentless battlefield,

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.200
their sights set on a major victory.

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:59.580
D-Do you mean... no! Can it be?

00:01:59.580 --> 00:02:01.370
I-I'm afraid so...

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.450
Uh-oh...

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.120
Armored Gi chariots!

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:10.410
Shit! Hey, you! Get outta there!

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:16.750
War chariots, of all things!

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:18.080
Protect our commander!

00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:20.660
Never mind me--protect the infantry!

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:25.120
War chariots, in this smoke? Now what?

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:26.750
How can we...

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.750
Shin.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:30.370
There's only one--

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:33.870
Only one way through this.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.620
"The Hi Shin Unit Retaliates"

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:02.290
There's a thrill to war
that really has no equal.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:05.700
For a strategist, it's using your own brain

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.450
to manipulate the fighting of a multitude

00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:11.750
into a one-sided slaughter.

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:16.700
Indeed, Gen Pou's strategies
controlled the battlefield

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:18.870
as though war were a board game,

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:22.160
dispatching Chin troops with great efficiency.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:26.700
Behind the smokescreen,
the once-confused Gi troops

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:31.250
were divided up into
several zones and repositioned.

00:03:31.250 --> 00:03:34.830
Next, the archers attacked the Chin troops,
while at the same time

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:38.700
herding them to crowd together
in a straight line--

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:44.040
a "road" of Chin soldiers down
which the chariot squadron barreled.

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.040
Of course, the smoke-blinded Chin troops

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:49.750
were completely unaware of all of this.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:55.330
When the war chariots attacked
thick and fast, they could only take it.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.620
Behind this great smokescreen,
unfathomable both inside and out,

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:03.910
rose up a horrific mountain
of Chin's dead and wounded.

00:04:06.620 --> 00:04:08.830
Kyou Kai! What's your plan?

00:04:16.450 --> 00:04:17.450
Jump!

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:26.000
Shin!

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.330
Tighten your defenses--and focus on Shin!

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.500
They're using sound to confuse us.

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:38.120
You must have heard that
occasional high-pitched bell.

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:41.750
That's giving our position to the archers
and the chariot squadron.

00:04:44.330 --> 00:04:46.040
It's the rhythm!

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:51.870
Right. If we put out a similar sound,
we can disrupt their communication.

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:54.200
All right.

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:57.790
First have everyone find things
that make that kind of sound,

00:04:57.790 --> 00:04:59.750
then bang 'em for all you're worth!

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:04.750
I just noticed an entirely
different sound--low and booming.

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:06.620
What could that be?

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:08.410
Another signal?

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:12.040
Sounds like a gong.
Probably a signal from the main forces.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:15.250
It must be providing even greater direction.

00:05:16.700 --> 00:05:17.700
Kyou Kai!

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:22.370
Did you just say it's a signal
from the main forces?

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.540
So in other words...

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:32.000
wherever that sound is comin' from
is where their main forces are?!

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.450
Don't tell me...

00:05:37.450 --> 00:05:40.450
He means to strike the main forces?!

00:05:40.450 --> 00:05:42.500
It won't work.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:49.290
You can't pin down the source of that gong,
not in all this smoke and racket.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.660
Aren't you forgettin' something, Kyou Kai?

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:54.120
Or should I say, some <i>one</i> ?

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:01.000
You called, Commander?

00:06:03.790 --> 00:06:06.000
The Sei Seikii!

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.750
Seikii! You live in the mountains--you <i>gotta</i>
have sharper ears than we do!

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:16.830
See if any of your buddies knows
where that gong sound is comin' from!

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:18.580
Do you even have to ask?

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:21.540
They call me "He Who Hears Wingbeats"!

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:23.940
"Seikii: Sergeant"

00:06:21.540 --> 00:06:25.330
If that's where you're headed,
he with the best hearing in the tribe

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:27.700
will lead the way!

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:28.950
All right!

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:32.290
We'll take the cavalry. So Sui, round 'em up!

00:06:32.290 --> 00:06:35.660
Sorry, En--can you stay here
and handle the infantry?

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.540
Absolutely.

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:40.040
W-Wait, Shin, sir!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.370
We in the cavalry number only 150.

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:48.450
I can't imagine how much bigger
the enemy's main forces must be.

00:06:48.450 --> 00:06:52.410
If we make it that far and can't break through,

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:57.000
we'll never be able to make
it back here in this smoke.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.500
And if that happens,

00:06:58.500 --> 00:07:00.830
the Hi Shin Unit will be completely scattered

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.080
and plunged into crisis.

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:05.250
We should ask for cavalry reinforcements!

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:07.870
Like we have time for that!

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:11.500
By the time they show up,
the Chin army could be history!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.250
But--

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:13.250
So Sui!

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:18.700
You said it yourself: a thousand-man unit,
a thousand-man commander

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:22.330
can turn the tide of battle.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.200
That time is now!

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:27.910
We can lead this battle
to victory with our own hands!

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:38.580
It looks like I can't stop you.

00:07:38.580 --> 00:07:42.500
Nope. If you all won't go, I will.
Hell, I'll go alone.

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.870
Very funny.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:49.620
We are the Hi Shin Unit.
We go with our commander

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:52.000
even into the very jaws of death!

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:08.080
Mou Ten, sir, won't our
third unit be mobilized?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:10.750
I don't know the battle situation...

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:14.370
but they must be having
a rough time of it in all that smoke.

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.540
Hard to say...

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:21.500
Since we can't see inside, we can't
tell where to send reinforcements--

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:23.580
or how.

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:28.250
That smokescreen, though...
it's no ordinary smoke.

00:08:28.250 --> 00:08:31.080
If the Gi troops are fighting in there, too,

00:08:31.080 --> 00:08:33.750
the smoke must be made
of some non-suffocating stuff.

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.660
Anyone who'd bring something like that
to battle is a real piece of work.

00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:43.120
Grandfather's probably
thinking less about reinforcements

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.450
and more about whether he should
get the first and second units

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:47.750
out of there.

00:08:54.290 --> 00:09:00.120
Each Gi squad had soldiers
familiar with Gen Pou's sound trick.

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:06.910
This... this is no signal!
There's sound from the Chin troops mixed in!

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.910
Those bastards...

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:11.750
Signal the sound corps to change bells!

00:09:11.750 --> 00:09:12.750
Yes, sir!

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:16.580
What's <i>that</i> sound?

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:21.910
Th-The Chin cavalry!

00:09:21.910 --> 00:09:25.750
Look out behind you!
The Gi troops aren't exactly happy!

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:35.040
Don't stop! Onward!

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.000
This way!

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.120
Keep going!

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:47.580
The smoke's a lot thicker here!

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:49.910
We must be close to the source.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:55.750
This camouflage of theirs is gonna
wind up bitin' 'em in the ass!

00:09:56.500 --> 00:09:59.290
The moment we jump out of the smoke...

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:00.700
I can't wait to see the looks

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:02.660
on their sorry faces!

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:06.160
It's down to the number
of soldiers in the main forces.

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.370
Come see that for yourself!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.580
You'll see it shortly.

00:10:12.910 --> 00:10:14.910
The main forces

00:10:14.910 --> 00:10:16.000
are right under our noses!

00:10:29.750 --> 00:10:31.160
Idiots.

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:36.990
"Shin"

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.700
Gen Pou, sir--that signal!

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:46.500
I know, I know! Lay off, would you?!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:50.950
Aha... So some fool thought
he could take on the main forces

00:10:50.950 --> 00:10:54.620
with no conception of the power we possess.

00:10:54.620 --> 00:10:59.790
He must've thought he could
use this smoke to sneak up on us.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:01.830
But we heard him coming!

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:06.750
Naturally, my sound corps
deal in defense as well.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:09.700
That'll teach you,

00:11:09.700 --> 00:11:11.830
Chin fledglings...

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:14.120
The main forces

00:11:14.120 --> 00:11:15.250
are right under our noses!

00:11:17.830 --> 00:11:21.750
War is beyond one's control with might alone!

00:11:28.620 --> 00:11:30.000
Idiots.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:39.790
They found us out?! We should regroup!

00:11:39.790 --> 00:11:43.080
No, we push on through! Look!

00:11:43.080 --> 00:11:46.540
Their main forces aren't that big!

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:51.290
Got it! Shin, fall back two or three ranks
and let us take the lead!

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:54.120
What are you, nuts?! <i>I'm</i> takin' point--

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.410
<i>You</i> keep runnin'!

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:03.750
C'mon, Hi Shin Unit!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.410
Aha...

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:17.040
Aim for the soldier in front.

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.040
Yes, sir!

00:12:21.370 --> 00:12:23.450
Retsu Brothers, protect the commander!

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:31.500
Dammit! Who asked you, anyway?!

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.700
Don't you know who you are, bossman?

00:12:34.700 --> 00:12:35.750
What?!

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:39.700
If we lose you here, we'll be wiped out!

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:41.120
What he said!

00:12:41.120 --> 00:12:45.080
Now be a good boy and use us as a shield!

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.410
You guys...

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:53.120
Good thing we saved up for the
heavy equipment, huh, little bro?

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:57.540
Now, you miserable Gi archers... do your worst!

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:59.950
Focus on the rider out in front!

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:02.540
Fire!

00:13:10.200 --> 00:13:11.700
Keep your head down!

00:13:15.580 --> 00:13:16.540
Brother!

00:13:16.540 --> 00:13:17.540
Hey!

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.750
G-Go get 'em,

00:13:20.750 --> 00:13:22.870
Commander...

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:24.370
Brother!!

00:13:29.330 --> 00:13:32.620
H-Here they come! Archers, stand down!

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:34.330
Spearmen, front and center!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:37.580
Their infantry's out in front!

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:39.790
Like I care! They're goin' down!

00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:44.370
They're coming! Everyone ready?

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:49.080
Those imbeciles!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:16.120
Wha--What the hell... is that?

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.830
They hid that... in the ground?

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:29.830
There were so few troops
at Gen Pou's main forces

00:14:29.830 --> 00:14:33.660
because the man had an even
greater trick up his sleeve.

00:14:34.830 --> 00:14:40.330
Before the camp was a stake trap
meant to stop the cavalry dead.

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:42.000
With the debut of this device,

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.660
the Hi Shin Unit's front ranks
were almost decimated.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:50.080
What few soldiers remained were cut off
from their comrades in the back.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.040
Shin and his allies at the forefront wound up

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:59.330
being hurled in front of the
800 troops at Gen Pou's camp.

00:15:03.500 --> 00:15:04.620
Don't give up now!

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:07.200
I can see their general!

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:10.540
You don't understand.

00:15:10.540 --> 00:15:16.410
Morale is easy enough to whip up
for passionate pups like yourselves,

00:15:16.410 --> 00:15:18.790
but conversely, when your morale is shaken,

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:22.370
you plunge into the depths
of despair and stay awhile.

00:15:22.370 --> 00:15:26.830
It's an age-old weakness of troops
who rely on power...

00:15:28.250 --> 00:15:30.040
...and one I cannot bear to witness.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.290
Cut them clean through!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:39.830
So Sui!

00:15:48.660 --> 00:15:52.330
Damn it all... here, of all places...

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:58.830
Just then, and for only a moment,
the wind changed direction,

00:15:58.830 --> 00:16:02.290
and the smokescreen drifted
immediately behind Shin and his team.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:04.330
And then,

00:16:04.330 --> 00:16:06.040
in an amazing turn of events,

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:10.660
out of that smoke appeared the Gyoku Hou Force!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:15.370
What?!

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:25.700
I should be ashamed.

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:29.500
Ashamed to have let <i>you</i> get the jump on us.

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:31.160
Ou Hon!

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.080
Onward, Gyoku Hou Force!

00:16:33.080 --> 00:16:35.620
Don't be distracted by the small fry!

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:38.660
The general we're after
is right before our eyes!

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.200
Wait, you bastards!

00:16:44.200 --> 00:16:48.790
Inconceivable. There was no
signal warning of their arrival!

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:55.080
Aha... They must have exterminated
the surrounding sound corps first, then.

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:59.000
And in such a short time, too...

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:02.080
We might have a real contender here!

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:03.540
Damn it all!

00:17:03.540 --> 00:17:04.830
Commander!

00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:08.700
It's you! You're all right!

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:10.120
And you, sir!

00:17:10.120 --> 00:17:14.000
We used bodies as stepping-stones
to cross, like the Gyoku Hou Force did.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.330
All right! We can still do this!

00:17:20.540 --> 00:17:22.330
After the Gyoku Hou Force!

00:17:22.330 --> 00:17:25.080
That general's head is <i>ours</i> !

00:17:35.330 --> 00:17:38.870
Dammit! They just keep going and going!

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:40.910
Did our sound interference even work?

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:46.120
They've switched to a rolling sound
and a new rhythm, those rogues!

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:48.160
That means...

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.370
The third unit has been destroyed!

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:54.450
Now hear this, Hi Shin Unit!

00:17:54.450 --> 00:17:59.080
Just hang in there a little longer!
If we can just get through this...

00:17:59.080 --> 00:18:02.580
...I know our commander will kill
their general and come back to us!

00:18:09.160 --> 00:18:10.500
Shin...

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:20.120
We caught up to the Gyoku Hou Force?

00:18:20.120 --> 00:18:22.080
They don't have their usual strength...

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.750
It's likely due to Commander Ou Hon's wounds.

00:18:27.080 --> 00:18:30.330
Did that jerk go and get hurt?

00:18:35.700 --> 00:18:39.500
Why're you goin' all pale for
a little scrape, Little Lord Ou?

00:18:39.500 --> 00:18:42.660
How about providin' us a
little combat support here, huh?

00:18:43.700 --> 00:18:48.290
That brat! He has no idea
how deep my lord's wounds are!

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:52.200
You call that encouragement? You insult me!

00:18:53.160 --> 00:18:54.200
Sir!

00:18:55.370 --> 00:18:58.950
Ou Hon's in front! Go on, go!

00:19:03.250 --> 00:19:06.200
See? I <i>told</i> you...

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:09.250
If you think a battle
will go well on force alone,

00:19:09.250 --> 00:19:11.000
you're greatly mistaken!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:16.830
Fifth unit, sixth unit, advance!
Seventh unit, eighth unit, spread out!

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:19.700
Enemy garrison reinforcements!

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:21.410
Doesn't matter!

00:19:21.410 --> 00:19:23.410
Their general

00:19:23.410 --> 00:19:25.120
is <i>right there</i> !

00:19:25.950 --> 00:19:27.500
Enemy reinforcements!

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.660
I don't care! There aren't enough to matter!

00:19:29.660 --> 00:19:31.620
Just keep moving forward!

00:19:32.700 --> 00:19:35.200
A dust cloud, in the enemy's main camp?

00:19:36.410 --> 00:19:38.580
Are they changing formations?

00:19:40.750 --> 00:19:41.410
Commander!

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:43.250
Why, you...

00:19:43.250 --> 00:19:46.000
Go! We can make it through!

00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:48.620
Gen Pou, sir, preparations are complete!

00:19:48.620 --> 00:19:50.700
Look out! Something's not right!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:56.700
All right...

00:19:56.700 --> 00:19:58.160
...retreat!

00:20:08.200 --> 00:20:09.830
Th-They ran away?

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:15.620
What the hell? What about all these guards?

00:20:15.620 --> 00:20:17.580
Is this another trap?

00:20:21.450 --> 00:20:24.700
Sound the retreat gong for all troops!

00:20:24.700 --> 00:20:25.700
Yes, sir!

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:47.700
L-Look! The Gi army is retreating en masse!

00:20:49.120 --> 00:20:52.620
We drove them off...

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.000
We did it!

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:56.040
Yes! We did it!

00:21:09.830 --> 00:21:16.200
The strategist Gen Pou possesses
none of the military man's pride.

00:21:16.200 --> 00:21:18.120
If he gets cornered, he pulls out.

00:21:18.120 --> 00:21:19.580
Simple as that.

00:21:21.830 --> 00:21:28.790
Only after he judges his work
to be <i>mostly</i> done, of course.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:33.160
If I'd had my way,
I'd've trampled them a while longer.

00:21:33.160 --> 00:21:35.200
But no matter.

00:21:35.200 --> 00:21:37.290
The job's eighty percent complete, anyway.

00:21:38.450 --> 00:21:40.330
And if I ask for too much...

00:21:42.950 --> 00:21:44.870
...I'll die too soon.

00:21:46.450 --> 00:21:48.120
Gen Pou, sir!

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:02.870
Missed!

00:22:05.700 --> 00:22:09.040
Shin, wait! Don't be rash!

00:22:09.040 --> 00:22:10.910
Stay outta this, So Sui!

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:14.290
Our blades won't reach that general now!

00:22:14.290 --> 00:22:17.410
We've made them retreat--isn't that enough?

00:22:17.410 --> 00:22:19.450
Not by a long shot!

00:22:23.790 --> 00:22:26.410
So they retreated--so what?

00:22:26.410 --> 00:22:29.290
We lost <i>how</i> many of our men?

00:22:30.830 --> 00:22:37.250
They toyed with us... and left us in pieces!

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:41.040
Dammit... damn it all!

00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:50.700
Shin was right. When the smoke
cleared from the battlefield,

00:22:50.700 --> 00:22:56.660
the Chin army was aghast
at the sheer number of bodies.

00:22:56.660 --> 00:22:59.830
They had suffered a crushing defeat
before they knew it.

00:23:12.790 --> 00:23:17.950
The Chin army's big sortie
was a failure from the very start.

00:23:22.830 --> 00:23:31.370
<i>I'm dreaming of you, just like back then</i>

00:23:31.370 --> 00:23:39.830
<i>Trusting, unafraid of anything</i>

00:23:39.830 --> 00:23:48.080
<i>Your words that I always remember</i>

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:56.540
<i>Are getting fainter,</i>
<i>mixed up, about to disappear</i>

00:23:56.540 --> 00:24:01.500
<i>I go crazy trying to make them out</i>

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:05.830
<i>Barefoot still, I'd lost my way</i>

00:24:05.830 --> 00:24:10.080
<i>It's okay to stop</i>

00:24:10.080 --> 00:24:14.250
<i>But even if I go after you,</i>
<i>if I hold out my hand</i>

00:24:14.250 --> 00:24:17.500
<i>Don't respond just yet</i>

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:22.700
<i>But until I forget, don't change</i>

00:24:22.700 --> 00:24:26.870
<i>I ask this of you, and yet</i>

00:24:26.870 --> 00:24:34.200
<i>Like a long-awaited morning, it's starting again</i>

00:24:34.200 --> 00:24:37.700
<i>And I still remember</i>

00:24:52.000 --> 00:24:58.010
"Next Episode Preview"

00:25:02.000 --> 00:25:07.020
"Marauder vs. Strategist"
